{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/411482-list-of-loci","id":411482,"title":"List of Loci?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-19T07:54:15-08:00","id":411482,"title":"List of Loci?","content":"I'm looking for a long list of loci, either online or in one of the manuals.<br /> <br /> I don't need large, block descriptions, like the ones in book of spirits, merely short phrases.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://multiversalmoments.weebly.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://multiversalmoments.weebly.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2603-iamthenight","name":"iamthenight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T08:52:31-08:00","id":411621,"title":"","content":"\u2022 Artificial Resonances: Urban, civil, productive, communal, domestic, cultured, enterprise, success, avarice, ash, trash, memory, law, intelligence, artifice, contrivance, progress, architecture.<br /> \u2022 Elemental Resonances: Stone, earth, soil, water, air, metal, cold, heat, fire, ice, storms, electricity, light.<br /> \u2022 Natural Resonances: Wild, hunger, sensuality, nourishment, decay, fecundity, shelter, growth, death, nurturing, Summer, Winter, Fall, Spring, depredation, passion, fog, storms, rain, snow, drought.<br /> \u2022 Negative Resonances: Pain, fear, hunger, lust, disease, hatred, anger, violence, vengeance, grief, tyranny, mourning, disease, greed, ennui, envy, gluttony, pride, sloth, deception, pathos.<br /> \u2022 Positive Resonances: Endurance, bravery, hope, peace, love, splendor, sacrifice, nobility, compassion, justice, truth, beauty, honor, cleverness, majesty, integrity, forgiveness, patience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T09:17:07-08:00","id":411669,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much for your effort, but I'm looking for a list of LOCI not RESONANCES.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://multiversalmoments.weebly.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://multiversalmoments.weebly.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2603-iamthenight","name":"iamthenight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T10:14:17-08:00","id":411713,"title":"","content":"How much info are you looking for precisely? A locus can have any resonance, tied to an object in the physical world. So would you like resonance object pairings? Or the general terrain around the locus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T10:20:42-08:00","id":411716,"title":"","content":"I.E.<br /> <br /> The Old Tree: The site of numerous lynchings. Hatred Resonance.<br /> <br /> Telephone cabin: Used by many mine workers to call their families. Hope Resonance.<br /> <br /> Something of the sort. Bare bones stuff, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://multiversalmoments.weebly.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://multiversalmoments.weebly.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":2603,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2603-iamthenight","user":"iamthenight","date":". 02-19-2015, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2603-iamthenight","name":"iamthenight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T23:11:11-08:00","id":412456,"title":"","content":"I had an idea for a concrete pillar under a highway overpass, due to how water collects, yada yada, the road gets very slippery, and a lot of cars have smashed into that pillar, often fatally. The Authorities have tried to fix things, but the spirits that eat feed there nudge more cars into accidents despite the efforts. Resonance of Cars, Death and Destruction.<br /> <br /> Another one is a small memorial for a pastor who worked to get teenagers out of gangs, and who ultimately got shot for interfering. A statue was put up in a park close to where he lived, and it became a focal point for the Essence the people who honour him bring. Resonance of Courage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T05:43:46-08:00","id":415073,"title":"","content":"A few from some of my own games:<br /> <br /> - A locus of Death in the house's small garden, surrounded on all sides by the tall walls of the terraced houses around it. Here, in this untidy little patch of weeds and mud, is where a murderer buried his victims, one by one, until the Shadow side became a bubbling mire of muck, blood and sickly thorned plants.<br /> <br /> - A locus of Fire under the busy crossorads; a bomb fell here during the Blitz that started a raging inferno, one that roared through the whole part of town and consumed innumerable buildings. The embers were still glowing days later and, even when they rebuilt the road and filled in the great crater, the heat still seemed to seethe and sweat.<br /> <br /> - A locus of Plants in the broken old greenhouse, amidst a tangled mess of allotments and dilapidated old buildings here at the edge of the city. It's not just the verdant bounty of vegetation that has grown up here, twining through broken old glass windows and creeping up walls - it's the very act of reclaiming the urban landscape that has given this such power.<br /> <br /> - A locus of Madness in the old asylum. These days, the focus just looks like the collapsed, rusting old remnants of a bed, because the shackles and bindings have been removed or rotted away. Too many people here were tied down to simply scream their despair at the cracked ceiling; too many more fell prey to the unkind ministrations of the doctor who would, later, Change and become a Bale Hound.<br /> <br /> - A locus of Light atop the lighthouse, where the village slouches down to the cruel sea. Long centuries of the light's beacon shining out, a symbol of hope and of civilisation in the darkness for those sailing the rough waters off Cornwall, have imbued it with power; so, for a time, did the greed and fear of the wreckers who once prowled the shoreline waiting for storm-wracked ships to come aground so that they could pick over the carcass. In the Shadow, the lighthouse reaches far, far higher into the sky, a mad corkscrew of Escher-esque manner that bears the locus far aloft.<br /> <br /> - A locus of Fire amidst the roots of the blackened, burned old tree. During the Siege of Breslau, a stray bomb landed here amidst the woodlands, burning a great swathe of it down and killing much of the local wildlife. While the woods have regrown, renewed, the Shadow still bears a smouldering glade at its heart, where the spirit of the burned old tree still rules the woodland court, always bitter and pained from its wounds.<br /> <br /> - A locus of Metal in the junkyard, a twisted, melded-together pile of girders and poles that seems to have been fused by some immense heat. Where the junkyard now stands was once an old metal foundry; during its twilight years of a long, slow decline, the manufactory's fate was sealed when a fire raged out of control through the foundry, killing several workers and causing a partial collapse of the building. Where the fires were hottest, they melted even metal and forged the fused tomb over the corpse of the foundry owner, who died during the initial moments of the flame. He may have set the fire himself, driven mad by desperation at his impending financial ruin and hoping to claim insurance on the building.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}